WEBVTT

00:00:00.313 --> 00:00:03.398
On my way uptown, I count the doors.

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:08.274
The window keeps my face for a while.

00:00:11.713 --> 00:00:14.640
I can tell how late I am by the roofs.

00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:22.498
At the coffee cart, I watch the light across the street.

00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:25.883
[Traffic rises. A faint double tap.]

00:00:27.013 --> 00:00:29.483
When it changes, I go.

00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:36.500
At the top of the steps, the brass door is open.

00:00:40.513 --> 00:00:42.983
Lucky, I think.

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:50.921
In my notebook the whole trip fits on one line.

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:55.983
Brooklyn. Then class.

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:02.783
[Rail wheels, again.]

00:01:05.513 --> 00:01:08.537
What did I put in the space between those words?

00:01:15.513 --> 00:01:18.025
Same corner. Same light.

00:01:21.283 --> 00:01:24.083
[Two light taps, now clear.]

00:01:25.513 --> 00:01:27.983
There it is again.

00:01:32.513 --> 00:01:35.430
A spoon touches the rim. Twice.

00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:39.983
[A spoon rings twice against a cup.]

00:01:41.513 --> 00:01:44.452
There's another cup behind the one I took.

00:01:49.113 --> 00:01:52.222
The door hangs open for the length of a breath.

00:01:58.613 --> 00:02:01.637
Someone's hand is still on the other side.

00:02:08.713 --> 00:02:12.106
I remember the brass. I don't remember the hand.

00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:14.183
[A door hinge. A soft click.]

00:02:18.913 --> 00:02:21.781
If you ask how long it takes to get here,

00:02:24.713 --> 00:02:27.183
give me a minute.

00:02:28.283 --> 00:02:30.583
[Two taps in the distance.]
